# amlogic-lc618.config -- Kconfig fragment for the ARM-fleet 6.12 -> 6.18 port.
#
# Merged on top of arch/arm64/configs/defconfig by the kernel's own fragment
# rule (`make defconfig amlogic-lc618.config`) when a build names it. This is
# the BUILD-COVERAGE fragment for the fleet-port worktree: its job is to force
# every Amlogic driver being ported to actually compile, so an API break
# between 6.12 and 6.18 fails the build instead of being silently configured
# out. It is NOT the fleet's shipping config -- that stays
# arch/arm64/configs/defconfig, and reconciling 6.12-lc's defconfig deltas into
# 6.18 is a separate, later stage of the port
# (infra/build/arm-fleet-6.18-transition-plan.md).
#
# Moved in-tree from infra/build/configs/amlogic-lc618.config on 2026-09-08;
# the symbol set is unchanged.
#
# Grow this file as each driver is imported. Keep every symbol =m where the
# driver supports it: a module build exercises the same code and keeps the
# image small.

# Do NOT set CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT here. The 6.18-lc arm64 defconfig sets it =y,
# and forcing it =m demotes the WHOLE media subsystem to modules -- including
# MediaTek's two parallel vcodec trees, which then emit four pairs of
# identically-named .ko (mtk-vcodec-common/-dec/-enc, mtk-vpu) and fail
# modules_check. Built-in, those trees produce no .ko and never collide.
#
# ⚠ But this is a REPRIEVE, not a resolution, and the deadline is known:
# 6.12-lc's own arm64 defconfig sets CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT=m. That is the fleet's
# shipping value, so the defconfig reconciliation stage of this port will restore
# =m and bring the collision straight back. The duplicate MediaTek module
# basenames are therefore a SCHEDULED blocker with a decision owed before that
# stage (which tree is canonical, or rename one) -- not a latent wart that can be
# left alone. Do not read this comment as "the collision does not matter".
CONFIG_STAGING=y
CONFIG_STAGING_MEDIA=y
CONFIG_MEDIA_PLATFORM_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_V4L_MEM2MEM_DRIVERS=y

# Stage 1 -- meson vdec (wave420l's build dependency; it includes
# vdec_helpers.h from drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec).
CONFIG_VIDEO_MESON_VDEC=m

# Stage 1 -- wave420l HEVC encoder (SM1 / G12B). New directory on 6.18; nothing
# upstream to conflict with, which is why it goes first.
CONFIG_VIDEO_MESON_WAVE420L=m

# Stage 2 -- CSI-2 camera stack + ILI9488 panel (the lc618-media slice).
# These lived in a PRIVATE fragment while the four port slices were on four
# separate branches: their drivers existed only on lc618-media, so a sibling
# slice's build would have tripped the "fragment symbols did not survive
# olddefconfig" gate. All four slices are now cherry-picked onto
# linux-6.18.y-lc, so every driver these gate is present on the branch this
# fragment is built against and the reason for keeping them private is gone.
# They belong here, not in arch/arm64/configs/defconfig: this file is the
# build-COVERAGE gate (a missing symbol is fatal, which is what proves the
# drivers actually compiled), whereas the fleet's shipping defconfig is
# reconciled with 6.12-lc's deltas in a separate later stage of the port --
# which additionally needs CONFIG_TINYDRM_ST7586=m / CONFIG_TINYDRM_ST7735R=m
# that 6.12-lc's defconfig carries and 6.18's does not.
CONFIG_VIDEO_MESON_CSI2=m
CONFIG_VIDEO_MESON_CSI2_CAPTURE=m
CONFIG_PHY_MESON_G12A_MIPI_CSI_DPHY=m
CONFIG_PHY_MESON_G12A_MIPI_CSI_DPHY_ANALOG=m
CONFIG_VIDEO_IMX519=m
CONFIG_TINYDRM_ILI9488=m
